    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes along with the full build.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required emitting a welcome notification via the `NOTIFY` logger, containing the owner id and memberId, on successful owner create.\n\nI kept structural impact minimal by adding behaviour as a new, cohesive unit rather than growing any existing class:\n\n1. **New function class** `NotifyWelcome.java` \u2014 a single-method step (CC=1, no surrounding-class complexity) that logs to the `NOTIFY` logger. `memberId` is the owner's `customerCode` (the same source the response DTO's `memberId` field maps from).\n\n2. **Wired it into** `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted a `notifyWelcome` step between `auditEvent` and `respond`, under the existing `transaction` governance, so it runs on the successful-create path only.\n\nI did not touch the existing `AuditOwnerCreated` (large-context) class or any of the other pipeline functions. Two files touched (one new Java class, one YAML), each change small and self-contained.\n\n`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The captured log confirms: `NOTIFY - Welcome owner id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1`.",
